1
00:00:30,001 --> 00:00:32,421
That feels so good.

2
00:00:32,511 --> 00:00:35,181
I'm going to wash off all my fleas and lice.

3
00:00:37,391 --> 00:00:39,931
Hey. Don't just sit there in the corner.

4
00:00:40,011 --> 00:00:41,101
Come over here.

5
00:00:41,181 --> 00:00:44,061
You'll be eaten by a sea serpent if you fall in.

6
00:00:47,811 --> 00:00:49,401
He's ignoring me?

7
00:00:49,481 --> 00:00:51,361
He's no fun.

8
00:00:55,911 --> 00:00:56,911
In the Middle Ages,

9
00:00:58,031 --> 00:01:00,911
Danes living in Denmark

10
00:01:00,991 --> 00:01:05,921
who made a living as pirates, or thieves,
were known as Vikings.

11
00:01:11,881 --> 00:01:15,631
The Vikings had always longed
to live in England,

12
00:01:15,721 --> 00:01:17,721
a vast and fertile land.

13
00:01:19,551 --> 00:01:23,971
At the start of the ninth century,
the Vikings invaded England,

14
00:01:24,061 --> 00:01:28,941
and migrated into the northern region
as they expanded their power.

15
00:01:30,231 --> 00:01:32,941
However, in 1002 AD...

16
00:01:33,031 --> 00:01:33,861
Kill them all.

17
00:01:33,941 --> 00:01:36,951
the English army attacked the Vikings
who had immigrated there.

18
00:01:38,361 --> 00:01:40,741
In retaliation,

19
00:01:40,831 --> 00:01:46,461
Denmark began to dispatch troops to England,
and intensified its attacks.

20
00:01:50,331 --> 00:01:52,711
Following these political developments,

21
00:01:52,801 --> 00:01:57,131
the Vikings were thrust into a war

22
00:01:57,221 --> 00:02:00,391
to subdue the English army.

23
00:03:37,521 --> 00:03:40,441
THE JOURNEY BEGINS

24
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:42,491
Don't stop.

25
00:03:42,571 --> 00:03:43,951
Keep moving.

26
00:03:44,031 --> 00:03:44,951
Shut up.

27
00:03:45,491 --> 00:03:46,831
I'm rowing, see?

28
00:03:50,001 --> 00:03:52,081
They went out with a big bang.

29
00:03:58,171 --> 00:04:00,761
All right. Let's stop here.

30
00:04:00,841 --> 00:04:02,421
Stop the ship.

31
00:04:04,091 --> 00:04:06,181
VICINITY OF GAINSBOROUGH
THE CENTER OF ENGLAND

32
00:04:06,851 --> 00:04:09,681
What a pain. It's so hard to walk.

33
00:04:10,721 --> 00:04:13,191
And it smells terrible.

34
00:04:36,881 --> 00:04:37,711
Damn.

35
00:04:40,001 --> 00:04:42,881
These guys aren't army regulars, are they?

36
00:04:42,971 --> 00:04:46,591
The Danish army hires guys like us
for their own army.

37
00:04:46,681 --> 00:04:48,221
The Danish army?

38
00:04:48,721 --> 00:04:52,061
Are the Vikings helping in the war?

39
00:04:52,141 --> 00:04:56,191
Yeah, skirmishes with the English army
are breaking out all over the place.

40
00:04:56,271 --> 00:04:58,981
Vikings are incredible tools of war.

41
00:05:00,071 --> 00:05:04,861
The King of Denmark is going
to invade England someday.

42
00:05:04,951 --> 00:05:08,411
I don't know when it's going to happen,
but they're laying the groundwork now.

43
00:05:09,451 --> 00:05:12,871
You mean they're eliminating people
who stand in the way

44
00:05:12,951 --> 00:05:14,831
before the king sets foot on shore.

45
00:05:14,911 --> 00:05:16,251
That's right.

46
00:05:16,331 --> 00:05:17,831
If we assist,

47
00:05:18,961 --> 00:05:20,881
we'll be compensated well.

48
00:05:30,471 --> 00:05:32,391
There's so many bugs here.

49
00:05:32,471 --> 00:05:33,851
It's better than being cold.

50
00:05:33,931 --> 00:05:36,391
We got to earn a lot this time of year.

51
00:05:43,901 --> 00:05:46,321
Hey. Not bad, right?

52
00:05:49,451 --> 00:05:50,531
You're right.

53
00:05:50,621 --> 00:05:54,751
The English troops harbored by the lord
of this region are giving us a hard time.

54
00:05:54,831 --> 00:05:56,711
I have more than a hundred soldiers.

55
00:05:57,211 --> 00:06:00,251
My forces are greater than yours.

56
00:06:01,501 --> 00:06:03,711
The pirate's talking big.

57
00:06:03,801 --> 00:06:05,711
Don't say that.

58
00:06:06,261 --> 00:06:08,091
We're both Danes.

59
00:06:08,181 --> 00:06:10,261
Don't act as if we're the same.

60
00:06:12,011 --> 00:06:13,311
What did you say?

61
00:06:15,771 --> 00:06:17,271
Well, well.

62
00:06:17,351 --> 00:06:20,351
They're going to invade with full force
in coming years.

63
00:06:21,021 --> 00:06:25,361
In that case,
I think it'd be smart to move fast.

64
00:06:25,441 --> 00:06:28,031
None of you will die anyway.

65
00:06:29,991 --> 00:06:31,411
So, what do you want?

66
00:06:32,241 --> 00:06:34,161
Seven pounds of gold.

67
00:06:34,241 --> 00:06:36,911
And all the treasure and food the lord has.

68
00:06:37,001 --> 00:06:38,831
And we're taking all the women.

69
00:06:40,921 --> 00:06:42,251
Five pounds.

70
00:06:42,331 --> 00:06:44,171
As for the rest, it's yours.

71
00:06:46,711 --> 00:06:49,051
It's decided. Deal.

72
00:06:51,931 --> 00:06:54,391
What? What are they talking about?

73
00:06:54,471 --> 00:06:57,181
A job. They closed the deal.

74
00:06:57,271 --> 00:07:00,141
Great. Then it's time to eat.

75
00:07:01,561 --> 00:07:05,151
Well, then.
I will send another messenger tomorrow.

76
00:07:05,231 --> 00:07:07,441
I'll leave the battle plans to you.

77
00:07:07,531 --> 00:07:08,901
Don't run away.

78
00:07:08,991 --> 00:07:11,281
You have nowhere to retreat.

79
00:07:12,911 --> 00:07:14,911
And don't try anything funny.

80
00:07:22,831 --> 00:07:24,671
They surrounded us.

81
00:07:27,421 --> 00:07:28,461
Hey. Ear.

82
00:07:28,551 --> 00:07:30,221
You're so loud.

83
00:07:30,301 --> 00:07:31,931
Shoot. Shoot.

84
00:07:34,681 --> 00:07:35,931
It hit my ass.

85
00:07:43,191 --> 00:07:45,111
This will be good exercise after dinner.

86
00:07:45,191 --> 00:07:46,021
Kill them.

87
00:07:46,771 --> 00:07:48,531
Beat them at their own game.

88
00:07:51,701 --> 00:07:52,911
Shoot. Shoot.

89
00:07:57,871 --> 00:07:59,121
Damn.

90
00:08:10,461 --> 00:08:12,801
Try achieving something great on the battlefield.

91
00:08:13,471 --> 00:08:17,681
Then I'll reward you with a duel.

92
00:08:22,601 --> 00:08:24,441
Something great...

93
00:08:28,021 --> 00:08:29,191
Kid.

94
00:08:29,611 --> 00:08:30,941
Are you a pirate too?

95
00:08:43,541 --> 00:08:46,631
If you're angry, blame it on the blood of the Danes.

96
00:08:58,971 --> 00:09:01,101
Sorry. I didn't know you were alive.

97
00:09:03,181 --> 00:09:05,811
On the battlefield, the weak die first.

98
00:09:07,151 --> 00:09:08,561
Like you.

99
00:09:13,571 --> 00:09:14,401
Damn.

100
00:09:33,381 --> 00:09:35,221
Damn kid.

101
00:09:35,301 --> 00:09:37,181
Die.

102
00:11:12,521 --> 00:11:14,231
You bastard.

103
00:11:23,571 --> 00:11:25,701
You're starting to look like a fighter.

104
00:11:39,171 --> 00:11:40,761
Hey, Thorfinn.

105
00:11:40,841 --> 00:11:42,971
Can you go scout for a bit?

106
00:11:43,971 --> 00:11:46,261
What? Why do I have to go?

107
00:12:02,321 --> 00:12:04,111
Kid. How dare you?

108
00:12:06,411 --> 00:12:07,871
Hold him down.

109
00:12:07,951 --> 00:12:09,331
I'm going to kill him.

110
00:12:36,101 --> 00:12:37,061
There he is.

111
00:12:37,151 --> 00:12:38,521
Over there.

112
00:12:58,041 --> 00:12:59,961
Over there. Don't let him get away.

113
00:13:21,901 --> 00:13:25,991
You know, I think the present king is a fool.

114
00:13:26,071 --> 00:13:29,121
Mom. Don't say that out loud.

115
00:13:29,201 --> 00:13:32,161
King Edgar from two generations ago was good.

116
00:13:32,241 --> 00:13:34,291
He made friends with the Danes.

117
00:13:35,331 --> 00:13:37,751
Everyone respected him.

118
00:13:37,831 --> 00:13:40,421
He was a good Christian.

119
00:13:42,961 --> 00:13:46,301
But the reigning king, King Ethelred, is no good.

120
00:13:46,381 --> 00:13:50,101
He suddenly killed all the Danes in the country.

121
00:13:51,681 --> 00:13:54,471
Of course they'd be mad.

122
00:13:54,561 --> 00:13:55,641
Mom.

123
00:13:55,731 --> 00:13:58,901
Don't say that in front of other people.

124
00:13:58,981 --> 00:14:01,521
If a soldier overheard you...

125
00:14:04,611 --> 00:14:07,321
Mom. Come over here. Mom.

126
00:14:09,951 --> 00:14:13,951
1008 AD
EAST ANGLIA THE EAST OF ENGLAND

127
00:14:42,861 --> 00:14:43,821
You're awake.

128
00:14:45,571 --> 00:14:48,651
We were just about to eat dinner.

129
00:14:48,741 --> 00:14:50,361
How are your wounds?

130
00:14:52,201 --> 00:14:54,531
I washed your clothes.

131
00:14:54,621 --> 00:14:56,081
Wear that instead.

132
00:14:59,831 --> 00:15:01,581
Your dagger is right there.

133
00:15:03,541 --> 00:15:05,921
These clothes might be too big.

134
00:15:06,711 --> 00:15:09,091
These are the only men's clothes I have.

135
00:15:11,011 --> 00:15:13,851
Okay, sit down. You're hungry, right?

136
00:15:27,151 --> 00:15:30,151
You must have been starving.

137
00:15:30,241 --> 00:15:31,701
What's your name?

138
00:15:31,781 --> 00:15:33,071
Where did you come from?

139
00:15:33,781 --> 00:15:35,491
What happened to your family?

140
00:15:37,621 --> 00:15:40,871
See? He doesn't speak our language.

141
00:15:40,961 --> 00:15:42,791
Maybe he's a Dane.

142
00:15:42,871 --> 00:15:44,131
What are you trying to say?

143
00:15:45,211 --> 00:15:46,541
No matter where he's from,

144
00:15:46,631 --> 00:15:51,261
Jesus would never forgive me
for leaving an injured child lying there on the ground.

145
00:15:52,301 --> 00:15:53,471
But still,

146
00:15:53,551 --> 00:15:56,681
the Danes are the enemy of the English, right?

147
00:15:56,761 --> 00:16:01,271
Dad's serving in the military,
because the Danes attacked us.

148
00:16:02,441 --> 00:16:04,191
What's your point?

149
00:16:05,231 --> 00:16:09,981
Women and children are not obligated
to get involved in a quarrel among men.

150
00:16:10,071 --> 00:16:12,151
Maybe that's true, but still...

151
00:16:24,581 --> 00:16:26,211
He's covered in fleas.

152
00:16:26,291 --> 00:16:29,551
Stop scratching. They're getting in the food.

153
00:16:37,051 --> 00:16:38,511
See?

154
00:16:38,601 --> 00:16:40,601
Doesn't that feel better?

155
00:16:40,681 --> 00:16:44,351
Boys are such slobs.

156
00:16:44,441 --> 00:16:47,941
My youngest son used to scratch his head a lot too.

157
00:16:48,861 --> 00:16:51,991
Whenever he did that, I'd comb his hair.

158
00:16:54,821 --> 00:16:58,621
He caught a cold and died two years ago.

159
00:17:03,201 --> 00:17:05,461
I can't understand what you're saying.

160
00:17:08,211 --> 00:17:11,091
I'm not English.

161
00:17:16,681 --> 00:17:17,971
What?

162
00:17:18,051 --> 00:17:20,391
So, you can speak after all.

163
00:17:32,731 --> 00:17:34,491
Hey, woman.

164
00:17:34,571 --> 00:17:36,151
Yes? What is it?

165
00:17:36,701 --> 00:17:39,821
A Danish scout is hiding out in the area.

166
00:17:39,911 --> 00:17:42,241
Have you seen a suspicious-looking kid?

167
00:17:43,291 --> 00:17:46,161
A kid? You mean, a child pirate?

168
00:17:47,081 --> 00:17:48,671
Yes, but don't underestimate him.

169
00:17:48,751 --> 00:17:52,341
He killed two of His Highness' soldiers.

170
00:17:52,421 --> 00:17:54,881
He has an arrow wound on his left arm.

171
00:18:06,601 --> 00:18:09,901
Woman. Is that your kid?

172
00:18:09,981 --> 00:18:11,151
Yes, he is.

173
00:18:11,651 --> 00:18:14,401
He's my youngest, John. Is something wrong?

174
00:18:18,031 --> 00:18:20,991
He's the same height as that kid.

175
00:18:21,071 --> 00:18:22,621
If you see him, notify us.

176
00:18:32,791 --> 00:18:34,671
Do you understand what you're doing?

177
00:18:35,551 --> 00:18:37,421
He's a pirate.

178
00:18:37,881 --> 00:18:41,091
He killed two people. Even though he's only a kid.

179
00:18:41,181 --> 00:18:43,101
Why are you hiding him?

180
00:18:44,471 --> 00:18:47,641
It's not normal for a kid to be a pirate.

181
00:18:47,731 --> 00:18:49,191
Something must have happened.

182
00:18:49,731 --> 00:18:52,401
Something must have happened? So what?

183
00:18:52,481 --> 00:18:55,021
That's not what I'm talking about.

184
00:18:55,111 --> 00:18:58,191
He can't replace John.

185
00:19:02,571 --> 00:19:04,831
I'm going to go see the soldier.

186
00:19:18,591 --> 00:19:19,421
R--

187
00:19:20,341 --> 00:19:21,341
Run.

188
00:19:24,431 --> 00:19:25,721
Wait.

189
00:19:33,611 --> 00:19:34,611
John.

190
00:19:47,201 --> 00:19:48,911
Do you see a sign from Thorfinn?

191
00:19:49,001 --> 00:19:51,081
It should be coming any time now.

192
00:19:51,161 --> 00:19:52,001
I see it.

193
00:19:52,791 --> 00:19:53,831
Over there.

194
00:20:01,881 --> 00:20:02,841
There's a fire.

195
00:20:02,931 --> 00:20:04,761
The cottage on the beach is burning.

196
00:20:05,431 --> 00:20:07,141
Men. Come here.

197
00:20:07,221 --> 00:20:08,261
Hurry.

198
00:20:08,931 --> 00:20:10,931
Bring the buckets. The buckets.

199
00:20:23,201 --> 00:20:24,611
I knew it.

200
00:20:27,031 --> 00:20:29,081
So, you were disguising yourself.

201
00:20:37,421 --> 00:20:39,631
Hey. What's that?

202
00:20:43,801 --> 00:20:45,011
How terrible.

203
00:20:59,321 --> 00:21:00,151
Damn it.

204
00:21:00,531 --> 00:21:02,611
Who is that kid?

205
00:21:02,691 --> 00:21:04,401
Did he kill him?

206
00:21:21,091 --> 00:21:22,631
Why are you here?

207
00:21:22,711 --> 00:21:24,171
I told you to run away.

208
00:21:24,261 --> 00:21:26,181
I told you in English.

209
00:21:26,261 --> 00:21:27,181
He's coming this way.

210
00:21:28,051 --> 00:21:30,301
There's still time. Run to the forest.

211
00:21:30,391 --> 00:21:32,061
Get far away from the ocean.

212
00:21:32,141 --> 00:21:33,641
Hurry, or else they'll...

213
00:21:41,481 --> 00:21:43,441
Hey. What's that?

214
00:21:54,081 --> 00:21:55,461
No...

215
00:21:55,541 --> 00:21:56,961
Run.

216
00:21:57,621 --> 00:21:58,751
Forget about the fire.

217
00:21:59,461 --> 00:22:01,171
Everyone, run.

218
00:22:02,381 --> 00:22:05,591
The Vikings are here.

219
00:22:15,311 --> 00:22:17,771
Hey. Good job, Thorfinn.

220
00:22:18,561 --> 00:22:21,191
This village is doing better than I thought.

221
00:22:22,361 --> 00:22:24,191
Don't mess around.

222
00:22:24,281 --> 00:22:26,651
Finish them before the enemy arrives.
